{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966785,"nonce":"Fv6zcBTDt3VjFZAsWNeycgRt4mI=","title":"cn::context_menu / popover / dropdown surface BG stuck at opacity 0 on canvas-bearing pages","message":"`KeyframeProperties::is_composite_promotable()` ([`blinc_animation/src/keyframe.rs`](crates/blinc_animation/src/keyframe.rs)) early-returned `false` whenever `rotate.is_some()`, regardless of whether the value was identity. The CSS `@keyframes` parser at `style_to_keyframe_properties` ([`blinc_layout/src/css_parser.rs`](crates/blinc_layout/src/css_parser.rs)) deliberately fills `rotate = Some(style.rotate.unwrap_or(0.0))` whenever ANY transform component is set on the keyframe — a `lerp_opt` consistency invariant so interpolating between two keyframes can't jump between `None` and `Some`. That parser invariant means a translate-or-scale-only `@keyframes` (with no rotation in the CSS at all) still carries `rotate = Some(0.0)` in every sampled `current_properties`.\n\nFor `@keyframes cn-context-menu-enter` (CSS at `cn_styles.rs:1046-1049`):\n\n```css\n@keyframes cn-context-menu-enter {\n    from { opacity: 0; transform: scale(0.96) translateY(-2px); }\n    to   { opacity: 1; transform: scale(1) translateY(0); }\n}\n```\n\n…the parser produces `rotate=Some(0.0)` on every keyframe. `is_composite_promotable()` returned `false` → `compute_animation_status` did NOT insert the popover root into `composite_promotion` → walker's `pushed_for_css` returned false → primitives went to the static batch (not the composite scratch) → `apply_all_css_animation_props` did NOT skip the apply (the skip at `css.rs:473` is gated on `anim_props.is_composite_promotable()` directly) → interpolated opacity got written into `RenderProps.opacity` → SDF BG primitives emitted at color.a ≈ 0 → surface invisible. Glyphs emit through `render_text_*` which bypasses `RenderProps.opacity` propagation (see [`gotcha_tooltip_css_fade_text_invisible.md`](gotcha_tooltip_css_fade_text_invisible.md)), so menu item text remained visible. Exactly the symptom shape.\n\n\ncn_demo (no canvas) opens the same popover with the same CSS. It hits the same broken path. Difference: cn_demo's Frame loop ran the slow-walker through the bad path once and then quickly engaged the compositor fast path; the cached static batch held the post-animation steady-state primitives (opacity=1). Canvas-bearing pages keep slow-walking every frame because `had_canvas_painted` forces the fast path off — so every frame re-emits the popover's SDF primitives at the current interpolated opacity, and the animation never gets a chance to \"settle into\" the cache. Mouse motion incidentally triggered an invalidation path (`apply_stylesheet_state_styles` on hover) that landed at a moment where opacity was high enough to be visible.\n\n\nFour-target tracing along the entire chain pinned the failure to one line:\n\n| Target | Site | What it told us |\n|---|---|---|\n| `blinc_layout::css_anim_start=debug` | `start_all_css_animations` class loop | Animation IS registered: `class anim started class=\"cn-context-menu\" node_id=LayoutNodeId(20v1) stable_id=StableNodeId(...)` |\n| `blinc_layout::compute_animation_status=debug` | After `composite_promotion` commit | `anim entry is_playing=true promotable=false opacity=Some(0.033)` — found `promotable=false` despite opacity advancing |\n| `blinc_layout::compute_animation_status=debug` (verbose breakdown) | After `is_composite_promotable() = false` | `disqualifiers=[\"rotate\"] promotable_present=[\"opacity\", \"translate_x\", \"translate_y\", \"scale_x\", \"scale_y\"]` — pinned the disqualifier |\n| `blinc_layout::paint_routing=debug` | After `pushed_for_css` decision | `in_css_subtree=true composite_promotion_contains=false pushed_for_css=false` — confirmed the walker took the static-batch path |\n| `blinc_app::composite_css_overlay=debug` | Before jobs early-return | Showed zero `CssAnimated` entries in `dynamic_regions` → no blit attempt → empty log |\n\nAll traces removed once the bug was pinned. Re-add the same five if a similar \"promoted animation silently drops to slow path\" symptom appears.\n\n\n[`blinc_animation/src/keyframe.rs:is_composite_promotable`](crates/blinc_animation/src/keyframe.rs):\n\n```rust\nif let Some(r) = self.rotate {\n    if r.abs() \u003e 1e-3 {\n        return false;\n    }\n}\n```\n\nTreats `Some(0.0)±1e-3` as benign identity. A real rotate animation (`rotate: 45deg`) lands `current_properties.rotate` well above the threshold and correctly takes the slow path. At the instant a real rotate animation crosses zero, the texture briefly promotes; rendered output matches the slow-path output at that point (zero rotation = identity), so there's no visible discontinuity.\n\nRegression tests in `composite_promotable_tests`:\n- `identity_rotate_is_benign` — covers the cn-context-menu shape (opacity + scale + translateY + rotate=Some(0.0))\n- `near_zero_rotate_within_epsilon_is_benign` — covers lerp drift between two Some(0.0) endpoints\n\nThe existing `rotate_disqualifies_pending_shader_support` test uses `rotate: Some(45.0)` which is well above the epsilon and still rejects correctly.\n\n\n- **Phase-1 `invalidate_overlay_mount_textures` hook at windowed.rs:5845.** `dynamic_regions` is cleared and repopulated by the walker (Phase 4), so at Phase 1 the map still holds the PREVIOUS frame's entries. The hook drops zero or wrong keys. Reverted.\n- **Two-bake confirmation via `composite_first_bake_confirmed: HashSet\u003cu64\u003e`.** Field, bake-site gates, and demotion/invalidate cleanup hooks all landed and built clean — but the bake is irrelevant: the popover wasn't promoted in the first place, the bake never received scratch primitives for it. Reverted on 2026-06-15.\n\n\n- [`gotcha_tooltip_css_fade_text_invisible.md`](gotcha_tooltip_css_fade_text_invisible.md) — explains why glyphs stayed visible while SDF BG went invisible (the same root cause: only the slow-path SDF apply honours `RenderProps.opacity`; glyphs emit at the text color's own alpha).\n- [`gotcha_composite_scratch_hash_layer_commands.md`](gotcha_composite_scratch_hash_layer_commands.md) — sibling case where the bake correctly captured but the hash dirty-skipped a re-bake; that path was correct, this is the upstream parsing.\n- [`gotcha_canvas_fast_path_freeze.md`](gotcha_canvas_fast_path_freeze.md) — explains why the cache never engaged on canvas pages.\n\n\nPromoting the popover to the composite path correctly fixed BG visibility, but exposed an inverted z-order: composite-promoted subtrees bake their SDF into a `LayerTexture` while text glyphs route through a separate `cached_motion_subtree_text_prims` pool (text is segregated from the SDF batch in `render_tree_with_motion`). Glyphs landed in the motion-subtree text overlay (dispatched at the slow-path callsite ~`context.rs:7704` previously), and the composite-CSS blit followed at ~`context.rs:7719`. Tree-order z-ordering inverted: opaque BG texture covered the menu items' glyphs at the end of the entry animation. User reported: \"BG renders immediately, glyphs disappear and only reappear once I move my mouse.\"\n\n**Fix.** Reorder dispatch at BOTH `try_render_with_compositor` callsites (slow path + CSS-only fast path) so `composite_css_layers_overlay` + `composite_motion_layers_overlay` run BEFORE the motion-subtree text/SVG overlay pass:\n\n```\ncomposite_frame\ndispatch_dynamic_batch_overlay\ndispatch_overlay_canvas_overlay\nrender_foreground_overlay\ncomposite_css_layers_overlay        \u003c- moved earlier\ncomposite_motion_layers_overlay     \u003c- moved earlier\nmotion_subtree_text_prims overlay   \u003c- now after composite blits\nmotion_subtree_svgs overlay         \u003c- now after composite blits\ndynamic_images / meshes / gpu_passes\n```\n\nThis restores tree-order z-ordering: BG renders first (faded by composite blit opacity), text lands on top.\n\n\nAfter the reorder, BG faded in correctly but glyphs snapped in at full alpha because the motion-subtree text dispatch reads `TextElement.motion_opacity` (which carries only motion-binding + RenderProps opacity, not the composite-layer's animated opacity — that flows through the blit, not through RenderProps, because composite-promotable animations skip `apply_keyframe_props_to_render`).\n\n**Fix.** Build a `HashMap\u003cLayoutNodeId, f32\u003e` snapshot of `composite-promoted node → current animated opacity` once at the top of `collect_render_elements_with_state` and thread the running `effective_composite_layer_opacity` through `collect_elements_recursive`. Multiply it into:\n- `TextElement.motion_opacity` (both push sites in the function — primary at ~6299 and segmented at ~6817)\n- `SvgElement.motion_opacity` (~6486)\n- `ImageElement.opacity` (both push sites — at ~6520 and ~6651)\n\nThe opacity multiplier ALSO threads through nested composite-promoted ancestors via `inherited_composite_layer_opacity * node_composite_layer_opacity` — composes correctly with motion-binding opacity, css-opacity inheritance, RenderProps.opacity. The lookup is HashMap O(1) per node, snapshot built under a single `css_anim_store` lock acquisition.\n\nWhy this works without breaking SDF paths: the walker's SDF emit (`render_layer_with_motion` in `paint/motion.rs`) is a separate recursion that doesn't read these collected `TextElement` / `SvgElement` / `ImageElement` fields. Composite-promoted SDF still goes to scratch → bake → blit applies opacity at composite time. Only the non-scratch paths (glyphs, SVGs, images) gain the composite-layer opacity factor.\n\n\nThe CSS parser's \"fill all transform components with identity for lerp safety\" approach is correct but over-broad: it fills properties that no keyframe ever sets. A two-pass parser (first scan determines which transform components are USED across all keyframes of an animation, second pass fills identities only for used components) would mean unrotated keyframes correctly carry `rotate=None`. The 1e-3 epsilon in `is_composite_promotable` works around this rather than fixing it. Worth doing eventually, but the predicate fix is sufficient for now.","files":null}]}